                        <labels>
                            <label>flr-improvement</label>
                            <label>pfl</label>
                    </labels>
                <created>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 03:49:58 +0000</created>
                <updated>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 13:19:41 +0000</updated>
                                                                                <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>4</watches>
                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="493847" author="JIRAUSER20216" created="Thu, 30 Apr 2026 15:00:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;If I am not wrong, this error comes from this block:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (comp-&amp;gt;llc_extent.e_start == 0) {
&#160; &#160; first_comp = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;;
&#160; &#160; args-&amp;gt;lsa_mirror_count++;
&#160; &#160; /* Most checks apply only within one mirror, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt; is an
&#160; &#160; &#160;* exception. */
&#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (prev &amp;amp;&amp;amp; prev-&amp;gt;llc_extent.e_end != LUSTRE_EOF) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; args-&amp;gt;lsa_rc = LSE_INCOMPLETE_MIRROR;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;goto&lt;/span&gt; out_err;
&#160; &#160; } &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;in llapi_layout_sanity_cb() function.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think we can add a new argument (e.g lsa_allow_incomplete_mirrors) and bypass this check, thus the split operation will be able to recover the file into a consistent state.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Does this make any sense?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493919" author="adilger" created="Fri, 1 May 2026 07:12:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=npapakonstantinou&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;npapakonstantinou&quot;&gt;npapakonstantinou&lt;/a&gt;, I was going to write that it isn&apos;t permitted to change the function signature for &lt;tt&gt;llapi_&amp;#42;()&lt;/tt&gt; functions, but I now see that the &lt;tt&gt;lsa_allow_incomplete_mirrors&lt;/tt&gt; is in &lt;tt&gt;struct llapi_layout_sanity_args&lt;/tt&gt; which appears local to that function.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is a bit sad that &lt;tt&gt;struct llapi_layout_sanity_args&lt;/tt&gt; is so poorly laid out, with &lt;tt&gt;bool&lt;/tt&gt; intermixed with pointers and ints of various sizes.  According to pahole:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
struct llapi_layout_sanity_args {
        _Bool                      lsa_incomplete;       &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*     0     1 */&lt;/span&gt;
        _Bool                      lsa_flr;              &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*     1     1 */&lt;/span&gt;
        _Bool                      lsa_ondisk;           &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*     2     1 */&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* XXX 1 &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;byte&lt;/span&gt; hole, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; to pack */&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;                        lsa_rc;               &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*     4     4 */&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;char&lt;/span&gt; *                     fsname;               &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*     8     8 */&lt;/span&gt;
        uint16_t                   lsa_mirror_count;     &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*    16     2 */&lt;/span&gt;
        _Bool                      lsa_in_parity;        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*    18     1 */&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* XXX 5 bytes hole, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; to pack */&lt;/span&gt;

        uint64_t                   lsa_last_parity_end;  &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/*    24     8 */&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* size: 32, cachelines: 1, members: 8 */&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* sum members: 26, holes: 2, sum holes: 6 */&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* last cacheline: 32 bytes */&lt;/span&gt;
};
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If there was any danger that this struct was exposed to userspace, the safest course of action would be to add the new bool in the 1-byte hole.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493930" author="JIRAUSER20216" created="Sat, 2 May 2026 13:56:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;So you think that we have to set the &lt;tt&gt;lsa_allow_incomplete_mirrors&lt;/tt&gt; flag always to true?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I noticed that about the signatures and I was thinking to do the same trick with&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;llapi_layout_v2_sanity()&lt;/tt&gt; function and have something like that for backward compatibility:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-c&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout_v3_sanity(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout *layout, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; incomplete, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; flr, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; allow_incomplete_mirrors, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;char&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; *fsname);

&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout_sanity(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout *layout, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; incomplete, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; flr)
{
	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout_v3_sanity(layout, incomplete, flr, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;);
}

&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout_v2_sanity(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout *layout,
			&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; incomplete, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; flr, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;char&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; *fsname)
{
	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; llapi_layout_v3_sanity(layout, incomplete, flr, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;, fsname);
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and in &lt;tt&gt;mirror_split()&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;lfs.c&lt;/tt&gt; we can directly call the &lt;tt&gt;llapi_layout_v3_sanity()&lt;/tt&gt; with &lt;tt&gt;allow_incomplete_mirrors&lt;/tt&gt; true.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493935" author="adilger" created="Sat, 2 May 2026 22:08:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It isn&apos;t clear for mirror split/delete if the &quot;sanity&quot; of the layout should be checked at all?  The file layout already exists and splitting off/deleting the partial mirror isn&apos;t making it any worse than exists today. Maybe only the &lt;b&gt;remaining&lt;/b&gt; mirror should be checked for sanity?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494006" author="JIRAUSER20216" created="Mon, 4 May 2026 14:17:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Since the goal is to remove the problematic mirror and return to the original state, I think that allowing&#160;&lt;tt&gt;mirror split&lt;/tt&gt; command to handle those incomplete mirrors, the goal will be achieved.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What do you mean with the &lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;remaining&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;em&gt;mirror should be checked for sanity&lt;/em&gt; ? During split operation or other operation?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494030" author="adilger" created="Tue, 5 May 2026 05:48:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I mean that it should be OK to split/delete the partial mirror, but if there is data that is not in the partial mirror then it shouldn&apos;t be allowed to split/delete the full mirror and leave the partial mirror behind.  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494035" author="gerrit" created="Tue, 5 May 2026 09:10:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Nikos Papakonstantinou &amp;lt;npapakonstantinou@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65672&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65672&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20011&quot; title=&quot;lfs mirror: Invalid layout: Incomplete mirror - must go to EOF&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20011&quot;&gt;LU-20011&lt;/a&gt; layout: Add function to allow incomplete mirrors&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 568c9b7c73010cc5d1a75b5c231b35f6c6a8dc74&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
